// Example: GPU kernel for vector addition
//
// This demonstrates the `kernel fn` syntax in Sounio.
// Kernel functions:
// - Are annotated with the `kernel` modifier before `fn`
// - Automatically receive the GPU effect
// - Cannot use IO, Mut, or Alloc effects
// - Must return unit type (void)
// - Parameters must be GPU-compatible types (scalars or references)
//
// Usage:
//   souc check examples/kernel_vec_add.sio
//   souc compile --emit hlir examples/kernel_vec_add.sio

